{"arrivo":"nb","origine":"non","origine_nome":"Old Norse","livello2":"gml","livello2_nome":"Middle Low German","n":69,"parole":[{"parola":"-ferdig","pos":"suffix","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Probably","significato":"Used for making adjectives from nouns: the quality of being ready for.","termine_origine":"ferðugr","catena":[{"codice":"non","nome":"Old Norse","termine":"ferðugr","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"verdich","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"non","nome":"Old Norse","termine":"ferð","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"non","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From ferdig (“ready”), from Old Norse ferðugr, probably influenced by Middle Low German verdich, in reality \"ready for ferd (“travel”)\", from Old Norse ferð, related to fare (“travel”)."},{"parola":"A3-papir","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"ereditato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"perhaps","significato":"A piece of paper in the standard A3 format","termine_origine":"pappir","catena":[{"codice":"non","nome":"Old Norse","termine":"pappir","categoria":"ereditato"},{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"pappir","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"la","nome":"Latin","termine":"papyrus","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"πάπυρος","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"egy","nome":"Egyptian","termine":"","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"egy","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"A3 + papir, first part is the first letter of the Norwegian alphabet with a number. Last part from Old Norse pappir, from Middle Low German pappir, from Latin papyrus (“papyrus, paper”), from Ancient Greek πάπυρος (pápuros, “papyrus”), perhaps from Egyptian."},{"parola":"A4-papir","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Unknown; perhaps","significato":"A piece of paper in the standard A4 format","termin