tegoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"gml","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Inherited from Old Norse reiðr (“roadstead, anchorage”), from Middle Low German rēde (“roadstead, anchorage”) and reide (“roadstead, anchorage”). Compare Danish red (“roadstead, anchorage”)."},{"parola":"rettferdig","pos":"adj","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"fair, just","termine_origine":"réttferðugr","catena":[{"codice":"non","nome":"Old Norse","termine":"réttferðugr","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"rechtverdig","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"gml","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Old Norse réttferðugr, from Middle Low German rechtverdig."},{"parola":"seilmaker","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"a sailmaker; a skilled craftsperson who makes and repairs sails, tarpaulins, fitted covers, and other textiles for boats","termine_origine":"-makari","catena":[{"codice":"non","nome":"Old Norse","termine":"-makari","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"-maker","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gmw-pro","nome":"Proto-West Germanic","termine":"*makōn","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gem-pro","nome":"Proto-Germanic","termine":"*-ārijaz","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"gem-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From seil (“sail”) + -maker (“craftsperson-forming suffix”), literally “sail-maker”. The second element -maker (“craftsperson-forming suffix”) is from Old Norse -makari and Middle Low German -maker. The latter is based on maken (“to make, do”), ultimately from Proto-West Germanic *makōn (“to make su"},{"parola":"skarlagen","pos":"adj|noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"sì","motivo_incerta":"Unknown","significato":"scarlet (usage as an adjective is rare; see the synonyms skarlagenrød and skarlagensrød)","termine_origine":"skarlak","catena":[{"codice":"non","nome":"Old Norse","termine":"skarlak","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"scharlaken","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"la-med","nome":"Medieval Latin","termine":"scarlatum","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"fa","nome":"Persian","termine":"سقرلاط","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"fa","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Old Norse skarlak, which came via Middle Low German scharlaken from Medieval Latin scarlatum, originally from Persian سقرلاط (saqerlât, “a warm woollen cloth”), a variant of سقلاط (seqellât, “scarlet cloth”), of unknown origin."},{"parola":"skole","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"ereditato","incerta":"no","significato":"school","termine_origine":"skóli","catena":[{"codice":"non","nome":"Old Norse","termine":"skóli","categoria":"ereditato"},{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"schole","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"la","nome":"Latin","termine":"schola","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"grc","nome":"Ancient Greek","termine":"σχολή","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"grk-pro","nome":"Proto-Hellenic","termine":"*skʰolā́","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"ine-pro","nome":"Proto-Indo-European","termine":"*sǵʰ-h₃-léh₂","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"ine-pro","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"Inherited from Old Norse skóli, through Middle Low German schole and Latin schola (“school”), from Ancient Greek σχολή (skholḗ, “leisure, free time; school”), from Proto-Hellenic *skʰolā́, from Proto-Indo-European *sǵʰ-h₃-léh₂, from *seǵʰ- (“to hold, overpower”)."},{"parola":"skrift","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"ereditato","incerta":"no","significato":"the act or manner of writing","termine_origine":"skript","catena":[{"codice":"non","nome":"Old Norse","termine":"skript","categoria":"ereditato"},{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"schrift","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gmw-pro","nome":"Proto-West Germanic","termine":"*skrifti","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"la","nome":"Latin","termine":"scrīptum","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"la","ambiti":["religione","scienza"],"via":"","testo":"Inherited from Old Norse skript (“writing, text”), borrowed from Middle Low German schrift (“writing, script”), from Proto-West Germanic *skrifti (“writing, scripture”), itself borrowed from Latin scrīptum (“something written; record”). Doublet of script (“script, screenplay; computer script”). Comp"},{"parola":"sperre","pos":"verb","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"to block","termine_origine":"sperra","catena":[{"codice":"non","nome":"Old Norse","termine":"sperra","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"sperren","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"gml","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Old Norse sperra and Middle Low German sperren."},{"parola":"stikke","pos":"verb","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"to stick, prick, stab, pierce, cut, thrust, put, jut (out), bite, sting","termine_origine":"stakk","catena":[{"codice":"non","nome":"Old Norse","termine":"stakk","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"stecken","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"gml","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Old Norse stakk, simple past of stinga, influenced by Middle Low German stecken and sticken."},{"parola":"stille","pos":"verb","n_etimologia":2,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","significato":"to set","termine_origine":"stilla","catena":[{"codice":"non","nome":"Old Norse","termine":"stilla","categoria":"non_precisato"},{"codice":"gml","nome":"Middle Low German","termine":"stellen","categoria":"non_precisato"}],"lontana":"gml","ambiti":[],"via":"","testo":"From Old Norse stilla and Middle Low German stellen."},{"parola":"storfyrste","pos":"noun","n_etimologia":1,"categoria":"non_precisato","incerta":"no","sig